Subject: [PATCH] T5 - slashing and insurance: 7 scenarios, penalty >= damage,
 fund never negative, mass-slash cap with deferred queue

T5 - Slashing and insurance (ECONOMICS_PLAN). Gate literally: 7 scenarios (single double-sign, repeat offender, correlated mass slash, fund exhaustion, penalty margin floor, mass-slash cap over windows, exhaustion and refill chain) with both invariants - penalty >= damage and the insurance fund never negative - checked at every step of the pinned run (87 steps, 48 incidents). Penalty parameters: T5_PENALTY_BPS 15000 (150% of the measured damage); insurance fund covers victims min(damage, balance), shortfall recorded, replenished by T5_FUND_SHARE_BPS 5000 of every applied penalty; mass-slash protection: T5_MASS_SLASH_CAP_BPS 500 of the registered bonded base (1 000 000 ALCRY) per window, excess penalty deferred - never dropped - and drained over windows (total_applied == total_penalty, pending 0). Golden digest 4cc9ea0319374c3c2c74bc88db6d7747b23f0e21ea637ae2270bc4c5707c9cef pinned in Rust tests and re-derived by the independent Python oracle (tools/t5_slashing_check.py), which cross-runs t5_slashing_example. NC: 7/7 named messages (tools/nc_t5.py; standard 6 + mass-slash cap, H6-H9/T4 precedent). 10 gate tests + 2 metamorphisms. Evidence docs/evidence/t5 (550 NCs cumulative over 22 phases). ALL GATES GREEN.
